{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786438114,"nonce":"v9TpgLbrWo421LaIg6sbOrBKHsg=","title":"The settings screens still hand-copy server bounds and enums in a dozen places","message":"**What is wrong.** Several settings screens restate the server's enums and bounds as literals instead of deriving them from `web/src/api/generated/`. Each is currently correct, so none is a live bug today — but this is exactly the shape that produced the `PoliciesSection.tsx` 422 bug, and it produced another one this week: `SUPPRESSED_REASON` had silently lost `snoozed`, so the dry run rendered a wire token where a sentence belongs. Both were found only because someone went looking.\n\n**The largest gap, and the one to fix first.** `PoliciesSection.tsx`'s priority `\u003cInput type=\"number\"\u003e` has **no `min`/`max` at all** while the contract says 0-10000; `name` (120), `matchers` (32), `reasons` (1-32) and `channel_ids` (1-16) are likewise unenforced; and the draft is **sent raw — never piped through `CreatePolicyRequestSchema`**. That is the original 422 bug's exact shape, still present.\n\n**The rest, each a real copy that currently agrees:**\n- `PoliciesSection.tsx` `REASONS` — 18 literals; a server ADDITION would silently not be offered.\n- `ChannelsSection.tsx` `VERBOSITIES` — the same enum is copied a third time in `tuningCopy.ts`.\n- `SourcesSection.tsx` `v.picklist([\"alertmanager\",\"grafana\"])`, repeated again as literal `\u003coption\u003e`s.\n- `SnoozeDialog.tsx` `SNOOZE_MIN/MAX_SECONDS`, `min={5} max={43200}`, note cap 2000; `Actions.tsx` note cap 2000, comment cap 10000.\n- `tuningCopy.ts` `MENTION_LIST_MAX = 10`, the `KnobKey` union (17 keys), and the option lists.\n- Untyped `Record\u003cstring, string\u003e` label maps — the same silent-drift shape as the `snoozed` bug: `DrillPanel.tsx` `STAGE_GLYPH`/`STAGE_WORD`, `DeliveryPanel.tsx` `REASON_LABEL`, `OccurrencePanel.tsx`, `RuleDrift.tsx`, `eventKinds.ts`.\n\n**The model to copy.** `TuningSection.tsx` and `SchemaForm.tsx`/`jsonSchema.ts` already do this correctly — every bound is read from the server's payload and nothing is hardcoded.\n\n**A caveat that matters for the fix.** `web/src/api/generated/validators.ts` is NOT yet a complete mirror of `openapi.yaml` — the generator had dropped `CommentRequest.body`'s bounds, so a test deriving only from validators can pass against a missing bound. Deriving from generated code is only as good as the generator, which is gate G4's job (issue 78d8553).\n\n**Done when.** Every enum-to-prose map is typed against the generated union so a new member is a BUILD failure rather than a rendered wire token; the policy form enforces the contract's bounds and validates the draft through `CreatePolicyRequestSchema` before sending; and the remaining literal bounds are derived from generated schemas.","files":null}]}